<title>CANADA: CBRS confirms British Columbia's ratings, outlook.</title>
<headline>CBRS confirms British Columbia's ratings, outlook.</headline>
<dateline>MONTREAL 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Bond Rating Service said on Wednesday that it had reaffirmed a AA+ rating for British Columbia's long-term debt and a A-1+ rating on the province's short-term debt.</p>
<p>CBRS also said the rating outlook on these securities remained negative.</p>
<p>&quot;Despite having a lengthy period of good economic growth, British Columbia remains the only western province that has been unable to balance its budget,&quot; CBRS said.</p>
<p>In the 1996-97 fiscal year, the province recorded another sizeable deficit, primarily due to a C$465 million shortfall in revenues, CBRS added.</p>
<p>((Paul Simao, Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8104))</p>
